  "description": "Photographs of plants in indoor public spaces (atriums, lobbies, malls, stations, libraries) are split into fixed groups of 20. Each participant is randomly given one group and sees its 20 photographs one at a time, in a fixed order, rating each for preference and relaxation (1–5). Before the photographs: background questions and the Nature Relatedness scale (NR-6). After them: affect (I-PANAS-SF), perceived restorativeness (PRS-11) and three intention items about spaces like these. Method replication of Ma et al. (2026), Land 15(5): 741.",
